The animal pens on the Kobayashi IV have held nothing living since you bought her, and you have been guarding them anyway. Your reasons are your own. The feed dispenser sits dead in the corner, its gears seized into one lump of rust, and you are slowly learning that it will outlast every part of the ship you actually need. You carry a stool in, set it facing the machine, and sit down to keep it company. Nobody else is aboard to see you do it, which is the only reason you do it. The dispenser, which has sat unrepaired through three owners, says nothing, and you decide that counts as loyalty.

