Vance carries an armload of berth-crew coveralls into the station laundry, where the dryers have gone quiet for the shift. He is taking over the job of a man who has not come back, and he has already told himself it is only until the rota is sorted. On top of the pile sits a stiff old crab-shell of a thing, a relic someone kept for luck, crusted and ancient in a way nothing aboard the Spire is. He works the tags loose one by one, then props the shell on the folding table, where it stares at the door.

