Years back, before the Kobayashi IV was yours, a younger Mira sat in a cramped transcription office on a station she never named afterward. She fed her mother's tongue, the old hauler cant, into a purge queue, one recorded phrase after another, because a client paid by the hour and asked no questions. The queue ran through a stack of ore-core samples, ragged and scattered across the bench, and she watched each phrase go without a flicker on her face. Only the last one she stopped, thumb hovering, and then she let it run.

