The gangway is down, and Vance Oduya stands at the foot of it with the berth logs under his arm, so you have taken the long way round the ship to avoid the conversation. You end up in the galley, holding a mug of reheated recaf and an old transit permit with your late captain's signature on it. You are mourning him in the most practical way you know: by correcting his spelling of "Kestrel" in red grease pencil. Beside the hatch, in the dim of the corridor, a shape in a hooded coat has been standing at the airlock window for ten minutes, watching you do this. You nod to it, and it does not nod back.

